<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39493" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pūlex</span></b> , ĭcis,
			m.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A flea</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 20,
				14, 54, § 155</span></i>; <i><span class="en">22, 20, 23, §
			49</span></i>; <i><span class="en">30, 10, 25,
				§ 85</span></i>; cf. <i><span class="en">id. 9, 47,
				71, § 154</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plaut.
				Curc. 4, 2, 13</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cels. 6, 7, 9</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Col. 8,
			5</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Mart. 14, 83</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>The ground-flea</i> or <i>spring-tail</i> (an insect that gnaws the plant ocimum), Col.
			poët. 10, 321: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">innascuntur napis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					19, 10, 57, § 177</span></i>
			.</div>
